  "content": {
    "id": "p99-q39-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "39",
    "prompt": "A swimming pool can be filled by a small hose in 7 hours, or it can be filled by a large hose in 3 hours. How long will it take to fill the pool using both hoses?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p99-q39-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "2 hours 6 minutes.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p99-q39-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Add the filling rates, then take the reciprocal to find the time.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Assume each hose fills at a constant rate and their contributions add. A hose filling one pool in $T$ hours fills $\\frac{1}{T}$ pools per hour.\n\nThe combined rate $r$, in pools per hour, is\n$$\\begin{align*}r&=\\frac{1}{7}+\\frac{1}{3}\\\\r&=\\frac{10}{21}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nLet $t>0$ be the filling time in hours. Filling one pool requires $rt=1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{10}{21}t&=1\\\\t&=\\frac{21}{10}\\text{ hours}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe fractional hour is $0.1$ hours, and $0.1\\times60=6$ minutes. Therefore, both hoses take $2\\text{ hours }6\\text{ minutes}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 56
  },
